{{also|drücken}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{recons|þrukjaną||to press|lang=gem-pro}}, {{recons|þrūganą||to threaten|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{recons|trūk-|lang=ine-pro}}, {{recons|trūg-||to press, beat|lang=ine-pro}}. Cognate with {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|drukken||to press, print|lang=nl}}, {{etyl|da|-}} {{term|trykke||to press|lang=da}}, {{etyl|en|-}} {{term|thrutch||to throng|lang=en}}. Closely cognate with {{etyl|de|-}} {{term|drücken||to press, push|lang=de}}: ''drucken'' is originally the southern form; the first German printers were in the south.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈdʁʊkŋ̩]|[ˈdʁʊkən]]|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-drucken.ogg|Audio}}
* {{audio|De-at-drucken.ogg|Audio (Austria)}}

